{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/fed_r_crim_p/0", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "fed_r_crim_p", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "553757", "offset": 1191, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "Yet Fed.R.Crim.P. 8(a) allows an indictment to join offenses of \"the same or similar character\", which describes two bank robberies.", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Fed.R.Crim.P.", "rule": "8"}, "metadata": {"pin_cite": "(a)", "jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "Fed. R. Crim. P.", "span": [4, 19], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/fed_r_crim_p/1", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "fed_r_crim_p", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "708182", "offset": 4730, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The narrow standard of review corresponds to the rationale underlying Fed.R.Crim.P. 33 that \"the trial judge, not an appellate court reading a cold record, can best weigh the errors against the record as a whole to determine whether those errors in the conduct of the trial justify a new trial.\"", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Fed.R.Crim.P.", "rule": "33"}, "metadata": {"jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "Fed. R. Crim. P.", "span": [70, 86], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/fed_r_app_p/0", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "fed_r_app_p", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "4161633", "offset": 963, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The panel unanimously concludes this case is suitable for decision\nwithout oral argument. See Fed. R. App. P. 34(a)(2).", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Fed. R. App. P.", "rule": "34"}, "metadata": {"pin_cite": "(a)(2)", "jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "Fed. R. App. P.", "span": [94, 112], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/fed_r_app_p/1", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "fed_r_app_p", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "1023269", "offset": 2318, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The plain language of Rule 4(a)(6) requires a motion to\n\nreopen be filed “within 180 days after the judgment or order is\n\nentered or within 7 days after the moving party receives notice of\n\nthe entry, whichever is earlier.” Fed. R. App. P. 4(a)(6).", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Fed. R. App. P.", "rule": "4"}, "metadata": {"pin_cite": "(a)(6)", "jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "Fed. R. App. P.", "span": [224, 241], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/tex_r_p/0", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "tex_r_p", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "2906123", "offset": 2940, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "To do so, we determine the evidentiary effect of American Express's petition and\naccompanying affidavit, which, if properly filed under Rule 185, may establish prima facie\nevidence of the alleged debt. See Tex. R. Civ. P. 185.", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Tex. R. Civ. P.", "rule": "185"}, "metadata": {"jurisdiction": "Texas"}, "reporter_normalized": "Tex. R. Civ. P.", "span": [206, 225], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/tex_r_p/1", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "tex_r_p", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "2906519", "offset": 645, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The trial court certified that this is not a plea-bargain case, and the defendant has\nthe right of appeal. See Tex. R. App. P. 25.2(d).", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Tex. R. App. P.", "rule": "25.2"}, "metadata": {"pin_cite": "(d)", "jurisdiction": "Texas"}, "reporter_normalized": "Tex. R. App. P.", "span": [111, 131], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/pa_r_civ_p/0", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "pa_r_civ_p", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "2307513", "offset": 2792, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "After completion of discovery relevant to the motion, a party may move for summary judgment when \"an adverse party who will bear the burden of proof at trial has failed to produce evidence of facts essential to the cause of action or defense which in a jury trial would require the issues to be submitted to a jury.\" Pa. R.Civ.P. 1035.2(2).", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Pa. R.Civ.P.", "rule": "1035.2"}, "metadata": {"pin_cite": "(2)", "jurisdiction": "Pennsylvania"}, "reporter_normalized": "Pa. R. Civ. P.", "span": [317, 336], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
