{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/us_const/0", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "us_const", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "1005412", "offset": 6974, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The Eighth Amendment expressly prohibits the infliction of \"cruel\nand unusual punishments.\" U.S. Const. amend. VIII.", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "U.S. Const.", "amendment": "VIII"}, "metadata": {"jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "U.S. Const.", "span": [92, 115], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/us_const/1", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "us_const", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "7023861", "offset": 2430, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The Court discussed in detail the due process clause of the fourteenth amendment regarding the limits of the State courts to obtain valid personal jurisdiction over a nonresident defendant. (U.S. Const., amend. XIV.)", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "U.S. Const.", "amendment": "XIV"}, "metadata": {"jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "U.S. Const.", "span": [191, 214], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/us_const/2", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "us_const", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "1446766", "offset": 6396, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The Commerce Clause of the United States Constitution gives Congress the power \"[t]o regulate Commerce with foreign Nations, and among the several States, and with the Indian Tribes.\" U.S. Const. art. I, § 8, cl. 3.", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "U.S. Const.", "article": "I", "section": "8"}, "metadata": {"pin_cite": "cl. 3", "jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "U.S. Const.", "span": [184, 207], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/us_const/3", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "us_const", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "2654061", "offset": 7825, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "The Constitution empowers Congress “[t]o define and punish Piracies and\n\nFelonies committed on the high Seas, and Offences against the Law of Nations.”\n\nU.S. Const. Art. I, § 8, cl. 10.", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "U.S. Const.", "article": "I", "section": "8"}, "metadata": {"pin_cite": "cl. 10", "jurisdiction": "United States"}, "reporter_normalized": "U.S. Const.", "span": [153, 176], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/state_const/0", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "state_const", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "4218221", "offset": 27252, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "Ohio Const. art. I, § 11. The Ohio Supreme Court has opined that this provision “does not set\n\nforth an accompanying cause of action for a violation of the right of free speech.”", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Ohio Const.", "article": "I", "section": "11"}, "metadata": {"jurisdiction": "Ohio"}, "reporter_normalized": "Ohio Const.", "span": [0, 24], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
{"id": "statutes-proposed/find/state_const/1", "kind": "find", "source": {"file": "vectors/statutes-proposed/README.md", "test": "state_const", "corpus": "courtlistener-10pct", "opinion": "2246952", "offset": 8953, "text": "after clean steps html, inline_whitespace"}, "provenance": {"status": "proposed", "drafted": "by hand from the opinion text, 2026-10-17", "note": "needs human review"}, "input": {"text": "A contrary holding would imply adherence to a philosophy of vindictive justice in clear violation of our state constitution (see Ind. Const. Art. 1 § 18.) and fails to be legitimized by any overriding state interest.", "format": "plain", "clean_steps": []}, "options": {"remove_ambiguous": false}, "expected": {"citations": [{"groups": {"reporter": "Ind. Const.", "article": "1", "section": "18"}, "metadata": {"jurisdiction": "Indiana"}, "reporter_normalized": "Ind. Const.", "span": [129, 152], "type": "full_law", "year": null}]}}
